win32u: Emulate display mode changes by default.

A game's resolution setting (ChangeDisplaySettings with CDS_FULLSCREEN) went
through winemac's real mode change. When the program wasn't the active app,
winemac set the Mac display's mode without capturing the displays, so the new
mode belonged to the whole login session and stayed after the game exited: the
Mac was left at the game's resolution.

Wine 11 can already emulate mode changes (the EmulateModeset value under
HKCU\Software\Wine\X11 Driver, or AppDefaults\<app>.exe\X11 Driver). Windows
programs then see the requested mode, fullscreen windows are scaled onto the
screen, and the driver's ChangeDisplaySettings is never called, so the Mac
display is never touched. This makes emulation the default; EmulateModeset=N
turns real mode changes back on.

Test: scripts/test-modeset.sh (demo/modeset.c).

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index eee8149..9b75c2a 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -166,7 +166,10 @@ static INT64 last_query_display_time;
 static UINT64 monitor_update_serial;
 static pthread_mutex_t display_lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
 
-static BOOL emulate_modeset;
+/* On by default: winemac's real mode changes set the Mac display's mode for the whole login session when the
+ * program isn't the active app, so a game's resolution setting stayed on the Mac after the game exited.
+ * Emulated modes are scaled onto the screen and never touch it.  EmulateModeset=N turns real changes back on. */
+static BOOL emulate_modeset = TRUE;
 BOOL decorated_mode = TRUE;
 UINT64 thunk_lock_callback = 0;
 
